Controller::initialize()
├── Given _initialAdmin is zero address
│   └── It should revert with ControllerZeroAddress
├── Given token is zero address
│   └── It should revert with ControllerZeroAddress
├── Given valid parameters
│   ├── It should set token address (eve)
│   ├── It should grant ADMIN_ROLE to _initialAdmin
│   ├── It should grant KEEPER_ROLE to _initialAdmin
│   ├── It should grant DEPLOYER_ROLE to _initialAdmin
│   ├── It should NOT grant DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE (inert in Controller)
│   ├── It should set role admin for ADMIN_ROLE to ADMIN_ROLE
│   ├── It should set role admin for KEEPER_ROLE to ADMIN_ROLE
│   ├── It should leave role admin for DEPLOYER_ROLE as DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE (never granted, so role can never be granted)
│   ├── It should initialize UUPS upgradeable
│   ├── It should initialize AccessControl
│   ├── It should initialize Pausable
│   ├── It should initialize ReentrancyGuard
│   ├── It should emit ControllerInitialized event
│   └── It should NOT set strategy manager (must be set separately via setStrategyManager())
└── Given already initialized
    └── It should revert with InvalidInitialization

Controller::receive() external payable
├── Given ETH is sent to contract
│   ├── It should accept ETH
│   ├── It should update contract balance (increase)
│   └── It should NOT revert (receive function has no restrictions)
└── Given contract is paused
    └── It should still accept ETH (receive function doesn't check pause)

Controller::provideExitLiquidity(uint256 _amount)
├── Given caller has KEEPER_ROLE
│   ├── When AMM is not set
│   │   └── It should revert with ControllerZeroAddress
│   ├── When amount is zero
│   │   └── It should revert with ControllerZeroAmountRequested
│   ├── When amount is valid
│   │   ├── It should transfer ETH from controller to AMM (via sendValue)
│   │   ├── It should update controller balance (decrease)
│   │   ├── It should update AMM balance (increase)
│   │   └── It should emit ExitLiquidityProvided event
│   ├── When contract is paused
│   │   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
│   └── When contract has insufficient ETH balance
│       └── It should revert with ControllerInsufficientBalance
├── Given caller does not have KEEPER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount
└── Given a reentrancy attempt from the AMM receiver (MockReentrantAMM)
    ├── It should reject the reentrant call with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall
    └── It should still complete the outer call (AMM receives the full amount)

Controller::emergencyExitToAMM()
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE
│   ├── When AMM is not set
│   │   └── It should revert with ControllerZeroAddress
│   ├── When controller balance is zero
│   │   └── It should revert with ControllerZeroAmountRequested
│   ├── When controller has ETH balance
│   │   ├── It should transfer full controller balance to AMM (via sendValue)
│   │   ├── It should update controller balance to zero
│   │   ├── It should update AMM balance (increase by full amount)
│   │   └── It should emit EmergencyExitedToAMM event
│   └── When contract is paused
│       └── It should still succeed (function doesn't check pause)
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount
└── Given a reentrancy attempt from the AMM receiver (MockReentrantAMM)
    ├── It should reject the reentrant call with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall
    └── It should still complete the outer call (AMM receives the full amount)

Controller::depositToStrategies(uint256 _amount)
├── Given caller has KEEPER_ROLE
│   ├── When amount is zero
│   │   └── It should revert with ControllerZeroAmountRequested
│   ├── When controller balance is less than the deficit (targetAmount - SM.balance)
│   │   └── It should revert with ControllerInsufficientBalance
│   ├── When amount is valid and StrategyManager balance is zero
│   │   ├── It should transfer full _amount to StrategyManager
│   │   ├── It should update controller balance (decrease)
│   │   ├── It should emit DepositToStrategiesCompleted event (with requested and actual amounts)
│   │   ├── It should return actualDeposited
│   │   ├── It should call strategyManager.depositToStrategies(_amount)
│   │   └── It should deposit funds proportionally to healthy strategies based on safety levels
│   ├── When all qualifying strategies have depositWeight == 0
│   │   ├── It should emit DepositToStrategiesCompleted(_amount, 0)
│   │   └── It should return 0 (unused ETH stays on the Controller)
│   ├── When StrategyManager already holds ETH (top-up path)
│   │   ├── It should validate only against the deficit (controller.balance >= targetAmount - SM.balance)
│   │   ├── It should send only the deficit to StrategyManager
│   │   ├── It should leave StrategyManager with exactly _amount before the deposit call
│   │   ├── It should absorb the pre-existing SM balance into the deposit
│   │   └── It should leave StrategyManager balance at zero after the deposit call
│   ├── When contract is paused
│   │   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
│   └── When strategy manager is not set
│       └── It should revert (external call to address(0) will fail)
└── Given caller does not have KEEPER_ROLE
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Controller::depositToStrategies(uint256 _startIndex, uint256 _endIndex, uint256 _amount)
├── Given caller has KEEPER_ROLE
│   ├── When amount is zero
│   │   └── It should revert with ControllerZeroAmountRequested
│   ├── When controller balance is less than the deficit (targetAmount - SM.balance)
│   │   └── It should revert with ControllerInsufficientBalance
│   ├── When range is invalid (endIndex > strategies.length or startIndex >= endIndex)
│   │   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerInvalidRange
│   ├── When amount and range are valid
│   │   ├── It should transfer ETH to StrategyManager (via deposit with indices)
│   │   ├── It should update controller balance (decrease)
│   │   ├── It should emit DepositToStrategiesCompleted event (with requested and actual amounts)
│   │   ├── It should return actualDeposited
│   │   ├── It should call strategyManager.depositToStrategies(_startIndex, _endIndex, _amount)
│   │   ├── It should deposit funds only to strategies in the specified range
│   │   └── It should deposit funds proportionally based on safety levels within the range
│   ├── When contract is paused
│   │   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
│   └── When strategy manager is not set
│       └── It should revert (external call to address(0) will fail)
└── Given caller does not have KEEPER_ROLE
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Controller::depositToStrategy(address _strategy, uint256 _amount)
├── Given caller has KEEPER_ROLE
│   ├── When amount is zero
│   │   └── It should revert with ControllerZeroAmountRequested
│   ├── When controller balance is less than the deficit (targetAmount - SM.balance)
│   │   └── It should revert with ControllerInsufficientBalance
│   ├── When amount is valid and StrategyManager balance is zero
│   │   ├── It should transfer full _amount to StrategyManager
│   │   ├── It should update controller balance (decrease)
│   │   ├── It should emit DirectDepositCompleted event (with strategy, requested, and actual amounts)
│   │   ├── It should return actualDeposited
│   │   ├── It should call strategyManager.depositToStrategy(_strategy, _amount)
│   │   └── It should deposit funds to the specified strategy
│   ├── When StrategyManager already holds ETH (top-up path)
│   │   ├── It should validate only against the deficit (controller.balance >= targetAmount - SM.balance)
│   │   ├── It should send only the deficit to StrategyManager
│   │   ├── It should leave StrategyManager with exactly _amount before the deposit call
│   │   └── It should leave StrategyManager balance at zero after the deposit call
│   ├── When contract is paused
│   │   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
│   └── When strategy manager is not set
│       └── It should revert (external call to address(0) will fail)
└── Given caller does not have KEEPER_ROLE
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Controller::withdrawFromStrategies(uint256 _amount)
├── Given caller has KEEPER_ROLE
│   ├── When amount is zero
│   │   └── It should revert with ControllerZeroAmountRequested
│   ├── When amount is valid
│   │   ├── It should call strategyManager.withdrawFromStrategies(_amount)
│   │   ├── It should receive ETH from strategies (via controller receive function)
│   │   ├── It should update controller balance (increase)
│   │   ├── It should emit WithdrawalCompleted event (with requested and actual amounts)
│   │   ├── It should return actualWithdrawn
│   │   └── It should withdraw funds proportionally from strategies based on withdrawal priorities
│   ├── When contract is paused
│   │   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
│   └── When strategy manager is not set
│       └── It should revert (external call to address(0) will fail)
└── Given caller does not have KEEPER_ROLE
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Controller::withdrawFromStrategies(uint256 _startIndex, uint256 _endIndex, uint256 _amount)
├── Given caller has KEEPER_ROLE
│   ├── When amount is zero
│   │   └── It should revert with ControllerZeroAmountRequested
│   ├── When range is invalid (endIndex > strategies.length or startIndex >= endIndex)
│   │   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerInvalidRange
│   ├── When amount and range are valid
│   │   ├── It should call strategyManager.withdrawFromStrategies(_startIndex, _endIndex, _amount)
│   │   ├── It should receive ETH from strategies in the specified range (via controller receive function)
│   │   ├── It should update controller balance (increase)
│   │   ├── It should emit WithdrawalCompleted event (with requested and actual amounts)
│   │   ├── It should return actualWithdrawn
│   │   ├── It should withdraw funds only from strategies in the specified range
│   │   └── It should withdraw funds proportionally based on withdrawal priorities within the range
│   ├── When contract is paused
│   │   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
│   └── When strategy manager is not set
│       └── It should revert (external call to address(0) will fail)
└── Given caller does not have KEEPER_ROLE
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Controller::withdrawFromStrategy(address _strategy, uint256 _amount)
├── Given caller has KEEPER_ROLE
│   ├── When amount is zero
│   │   └── It should revert with ControllerZeroAmountRequested
│   ├── When amount is valid
