Controller::setStrategyManager(address _newStrategyManager)
├── Given caller has DEPLOYER_ROLE
│   ├── When new strategy manager is zero address
│   │   └── It should revert with ControllerZeroAddress
│   ├── When new strategy manager address has no contract code (EOA or empty)
│   │   └── It should revert with ControllerNoCode
│   ├── When new strategy manager is valid
│   │   ├── It should update strategy manager address
│   │   ├── It should emit StrategyManagerSet event with (strategyManager)
│   │   └── It should NOT check pause status (function doesn't have whenNotPaused modifier)
│   └── When contract is paused
│       └── It should still succeed (function doesn't check pause)
├── Given caller does not have DEPLOYER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount
└── Given deployer has revoked DEPLOYER_ROLE from themselves
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount (wiring is now permanently immutable)

Controller::pause()
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE
│   ├── When contract is not paused
│   │   ├── It should pause the contract
│   │   ├── It should emit Paused event (with msg.sender)
│   │   └── It should NOT check pause status (function doesn't have whenNotPaused modifier)
│   └── When contract is already paused
│       └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
├── Given caller has SECURITY_ROLE on Registry
│   └── It should pause the contract immediately (no timelock)
├── Given caller has neither ADMIN_ROLE nor SECURITY_ROLE on Registry
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientCallerHasNoneOfRoles

Controller::unpause()
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE
│   ├── When contract is paused
│   │   ├── It should unpause the contract
│   │   └── It should emit Unpaused event (with msg.sender)
│   └── When contract is not paused
│       └── It should revert with ExpectedPause
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount
└── Given caller is not authorized
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Controller::version()
└── It should return "1.0.0"

Controller::eve()
└── It should return EVE token address

Controller::strategyManager (public variable)
└── It should return strategy manager address (automatically via public getter)

Controller::ADMIN_ROLE (public constant)
└── It should return admin role identifier (keccak256("ADMIN_ROLE"))

Controller::KEEPER_ROLE (public constant)
└── It should return keeper role identifier (keccak256("KEEPER_ROLE"))

Controller::Access Control Testing
├── Role management
│   ├── Admin can grant and revoke roles
│   └── Non-admin cannot grant or revoke roles
└── Initialization
    ├── Initial admin has all required roles
    └── Implementation contract is disabled

Controller::Fuzz Testing
├── provideExitLiquidity() within the valid range (0 < _amount <= balance)
│   ├── It should succeed and forward exactly _amount to the AMM
│   └── It should decrease the controller balance by exactly _amount
├── provideExitLiquidity() with _amount greater than the controller balance
│   └── It should revert with ControllerInsufficientBalance
├── initialize() with any non-zero admin address
│   ├── It should grant ADMIN_ROLE to the fuzzed admin
│   └── It should NOT grant DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE (inert in Controller)
└── upgradeToAndCall() with any non-admin caller
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount (ADMIN_ROLE gate)

Controller::Upgrade Testing
├── Given upgrade authorization (ADMIN_ROLE)
│   ├── It should allow contract upgrades
│   └── It should maintain state after upgrade
└── Given unauthorized upgrade attempt (non-admin caller)
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Controller::Proxy Testing
└── It should correctly point to implementation address

Controller::priceBatch()
├── Given caller has KEEPER_ROLE
│   ├── When AMM key is not registered in Registry
│   │   └── It should revert with RegistryContractNotRegistered
│   ├── When contract is not paused
│   │   ├── It should get the live base EVE price from AMM (eveBasePriceInETH(): live NAV / live supply; this batch is still equity)
│   │   ├── It should call exitQueue.priceBatch() with the price
│   │   └── It should price the current batch
│   ├── When contract is paused
│   │   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
│   └── When current batch is empty
│       └── It should revert (ExitQueue will revert with ExitQueueBatchIsEmpty)
├── Given caller does not have KEEPER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
└── Given reentrancy attempt
    └── It should revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall

Controller::processRequest(uint256 _batchId, address _user)
├── Given caller has KEEPER_ROLE
│   ├── When batch ID does not exist or user not in batch
│   │   └── It should revert (ExitQueue will revert with ExitQueueRequestNotInBatch)
│   ├── When request is already processed
│   │   └── It should revert (ExitQueue will revert with ExitQueueRequestAlreadyProcessed)
│   ├── When batch is not priced yet
│   │   └── It should revert (ExitQueue will revert with ExitQueueBatchCannotBeProcessed)
│   ├── When batch is priced but MAX_BATCH_PROCESSING_TIME exceeded
│   │   └── It should revert (ExitQueue will revert with ExitQueueBatchExpired)
│   ├── When contract has insufficient ETH balance (for ethToRedeem)
│   │   └── It should revert with ControllerInsufficientBalance
│   ├── When price slippage exceeds tolerance (finalPrice < requestPrice * (1 - tolerance))
│   │   ├── It should calculate ethToRedeem as 0
│   │   ├── It should call amm.processRedemption{value: 0}()
│   │   ├── It should NOT transfer ETH from Controller
│   │   └── It should mark request as closedDueToSlippage
│   ├── When price is within tolerance
│   │   ├── It should calculate ethToRedeem using finalEvePrice
│   │   ├── It should transfer ETH to AMM (via processRedemption{value: ethToRedeem})
│   │   ├── It should update controller balance (decrease)
│   │   └── It should process the redemption
│   ├── When contract is paused
│   │   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
│   └── When AMM key is not registered in Registry
│       └── It should revert with RegistryContractNotRegistered
├── Given caller does not have KEEPER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
└── Given reentrancy attempt
    └── It should revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall

Controller::processRequests(uint256 _batchId)
├── Given caller has KEEPER_ROLE
│   ├── When batch ID does not exist
│   │   └── It should revert (ExitQueue will revert)
│   ├── When batch is not priced yet
│   │   └── It should revert (ExitQueue will revert with ExitQueueBatchCannotBeProcessed)
│   ├── When batch is empty (no unprocessed users)
│   │   └── It should succeed without processing any requests
│   ├── When batch has unprocessed users
│   │   ├── It should process all unprocessed users in the batch
│   │   ├── It should call _processRequest for each user
│   │   └── It should handle slippage checks for each request
│   ├── When contract is paused
│   │   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
│   └── When contract has insufficient ETH balance
│       └── It should revert with ControllerInsufficientBalance (for first request that needs ETH)
├── Given caller does not have KEEPER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
└── Given reentrancy attempt
    └── It should revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall

Controller::processRequests(uint256 _batchId, uint256 _startIndex, uint256 _endIndex)
├── Given caller has KEEPER_ROLE
│   ├── When range is invalid (endIndex > unprocessedUsersCount or startIndex >= endIndex)
│   │   └── It should revert (ExitQueue will revert with ExitQueueInvalidRange)
│   ├── When batch is not priced yet
│   │   └── It should revert (ExitQueue will revert with ExitQueueBatchCannotBeProcessed)
│   ├── When range and batch are valid
│   │   ├── It should process only users in the specified range
│   │   ├── It should call _processRequest for each user in range
│   │   └── It should skip users outside the range
│   ├── When contract is paused
│   │   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
│   └── When contract has insufficient ETH balance
│       └── It should revert with ControllerInsufficientBalance
├── Given caller does not have KEEPER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
└── Given reentrancy attempt
    └── It should revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall

Controller::Edge Cases
├── ETH flow from AMM
│   ├── It should receive ETH from AMM
│   ├── It should accumulate ETH balance
│   └── It should allow distribution to strategies
└── Strategy manager configuration
    ├── It should allow setting new strategy manager
    ├── It should verify CONTROLLER_ROLE is granted
    └── It should fail if strategy manager doesn't grant CONTROLLER_ROLE
